the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the age is *a number*.
    the risk category is *a text*.
    the is_affordable is *a truth value*.
    the risk category or null is *a text*.
    the is_affordable or null is *a truth value*.

the templates are:
    the approval status include *an approved declined* with *a rate*.
    the approval status are listed.
    the approval status for *a number* and *a text* and *a truth value* is *a second text* with *a third text* under table approval_status.

the table approval_status is, with all matches:
    age   | risk category     | is_affordable | approved declined | rate
    >= 18 | "Medium" or "Low" | true          | "Approved"        | "Basic"
    < 18  | any               | any           | "Declined"        | "Standard"
    any   | "High"            | any           | "Approved"        | "Standard"

the knowledge base n0119_multi_collect_hitpolicy includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/0119-multi-collect-hitpolicy.dmn".

the risk category or null is the risk category, as stated in the model at decision Approval Status.

rule approval_status_2 with provenance the model at decision Approval Status:
the risk category or null is null if
    it is not the case that the risk category is a text.

the is_affordable or null is the is_affordable, as stated in the model at decision Approval Status.

rule approval_status_4 with provenance the model at decision Approval Status:
the is_affordable or null is null if
    it is not the case that the is_affordable is a truth value.

rule approval_status_5 with provenance the model at decision Approval Status:
the approval status include an approved declined with a rate if
    the approval status for the age and the risk category or null and the is_affordable or null is the approved declined with the rate under table approval_status.

scenario t001 is, as stated in "0119-multi-collect-hitpolicy-test-01.xml" at test case 001:
    the age is 17.
    the risk category is "High".
    the is_affordable is true.
    q_d_rel_approval_status expects answers ["the approval status include Approved with Standard", "the approval status include Declined with Standard"].

scenario t002 is, as stated in "0119-multi-collect-hitpolicy-test-01.xml" at test case 002:
    the age is 19.
    the risk category is "Low".
    the is_affordable is true.
    q_d_rel_approval_status expects answers ["the approval status include Approved with Basic"].

scenario t003 is, as stated in "0119-multi-collect-hitpolicy-test-01.xml" at test case 003:
    the age is 10.
    the risk category is "Low".
    the is_affordable is true.
    q_d_rel_approval_status expects answers ["the approval status include Declined with Standard"].

query q_d_rel_approval_status is:
    the approval status include which approved declined with which rate.

